# Check every text file out with LF, on every machine.
#
# Why this exists: the generators in tools/ build their markup in plain JS,
# so a joined block is always "\n" separated. index.html was being checked
# out with CRLF on Windows (core.autocrlf=true), so the block already in
# the file and the block the generator produced could never be equal, and
# `node tools/build-projects.mjs --check` reported permanent false drift
# on a clean tree. CI runs on Linux and saw LF, so the two disagreed and
# the local check was the one crying wolf.
#
# The blobs in history are already LF, so this changes nothing that is
# committed. It only stops git rewriting line endings on the way out.
* text=auto eol=lf
